{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2022_W16_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-16",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2022_W16_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-16.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2022-04-21",
  "report_week": "16",
  "report_period": "Week 16 (15th Apr to 21st Apr 2022)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Following the sale of the Kamsarmax \"Rosco Litchi\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) at USD 25 mill, Chinese owners now sold the sister vessel \"Rosco Palm\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 26 mill. Furthermore, the Korean built \"Derby\" 81/2011 Stx, Korea (SS 07/2025, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed for excess USD 24 mill. Remind you that three weeks ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Darya Kirthi\" 80/2012 Stx, Korea (SS 02/2027, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 25,25 mill basis delivery May-June 2022. Greek owners EuroDry have acquired the Panamax \"Santa Cruz\" 76/2005 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 08/2025, DD 07/2023) for USD 15,75 mill with T/C included until July 2022 at 14.800 usd/day. Note that the one-year-older \"Maribella\" 76/2004 Imabari, Japan (SS 12/2024, DD 02/2023) was sold three weeks ago at USD 14,9 mill basis delivery April-June 2022. In addition, the vintage \"Shao Shan 1\" 74/1997 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2022) from COSCO was sold to Chinese buyers for USD 8,6 mill. For reference, the one- year-younger \"Lily Breeze\" 74/1998 Nkk, Japan (SS/DD 01/2023) was sold back in February at the same price. On the Supramax sector, Japanese owners sold their \"GDF Suez North Sea\" 55/2012 IHI, Japan (SS 06/2025, DD 06/2023, BWTS fitted) for USD 22 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older \"Awesome Ashley\" 55/2011 Mitsui, Japan (SS 07/2024, DD 07/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at region USD 21 mill.",
    "tankers": "Idemitsu Kosan committed their VLCC \"Nissho Maru\" 300/2004 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 05/2024) to reportedly Greek buyers for region USD 30 mill. Note that earlier this month, the one-year-younger \"Tokio\" 306/2005 Mitsubishi, Japan (SS 02/2025, DD 02/2023) was sold at USD 31,5 mill. Eastern Pacific Shipping have committed their Aframax \"Banda Sea\" 105/2007 Sumitomo, Japan (SS/DD 05/2022, Scrubber fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 21 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Berica\" 115/2008 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at region USD 23 mill. Moreover, the \"Astro Sculptor\" 105/2003 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 01/2023) from Pantheon Tankers was sold at USD 15,6 mill. Remind you that the Japanese built \"Blue Power\" 106/2003 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2023) was sold back in March at USD 13,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low usd 9,00's fio range. A number of round trips from China via Australia into China were reported at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 22,000/25,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 25,000/27,000 pd. Indian trips via Russian Baltic into India were fixed around usd 55,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via North Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 27,000 pd. Continental trips into China were fixed around usd 34,000/35,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 27,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 1.7M. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China via Philippines into China with nickel ore were fixed around usd 29,000/30,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 25,000/26,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 28,000/30,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were reported at the level of usd 38,000 pd. US Gulf trips via Mississippi River into China were fixed around usd 34,000/36,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from West Coast South America into Continent were reported fixed around usd 26,000/28,000 pd. West Coast South American trips into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
